<title>USA: Commonwealth stake cut by Cumberland.</title>
<headline>Commonwealth stake cut by Cumberland.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cumberland Associates said Monday it cut its stake in Commonwealth Aluminum to 400,000 common shares or 3.9 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, Cumberland said it sold 200,000 shares between October 25 and December 17 at prices ranging from $15.125 to $16.705 per share.</p>
<p>Commonwealth is a Louisville, Ky.,-based aluminum rolling products maker.</p>
